course: dictionary
lesson: 14826
title: Quitter
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A quitter is a person who gives up easily, instead of trying hard or finishing something. The word can sting, because people use it as an insult. «Don't be a quitter, Sam. Finish the race!» Here the coach is pushing Sam to keep going.
explain: The clues are in the word quit, which means to stop. The opposite of a quitter is someone who keeps going even when things are hard. That quality is called perseverance. Coaches say «Winners never quit» to encourage players to keep trying.
explain: Stopping is not always quitting. «Ellie left the pool when the lightning started, because it was not safe.» Ellie stopped for a good reason, so she was being sensible, not weak. A quitter gives up for no good reason. A sensible person stops when staying would be dangerous.
fact: A quitter is a person who gives up easily instead of trying hard or finishing something.
fact: «Quitter» is an informal word, and it is usually negative.
fact: «Quitters never win» is a saying that encourages people to keep trying.
fact: Stopping something unsafe is sensible, not quitting.
fact: «Quit» can also mean to stop a habit, such as smoking, but this use is rare.
exercise: «Don't be a quitter, Sam. Finish the race!» What does quitter mean? | A fast runner who wins every race | A person who likes to sing | *A person who gives up easily | A person who lives by the sea
exercise: «Ellie left the pool when the lightning started, because it was not safe.» Was Ellie a quitter? | *No, stopping to stay safe is sensible | Yes, because she left early | Yes, she gave up on swimming
exercise: The coach says «Winners never quit». What does the coach want? | To try a different sport | To stop and go home | *To keep going and not give up | To sleep more
test: Find the word that means someone who gives up easily: «The quitter threw his bat down and walked off.» | bat | walked | threw | *quitter
test: Which sentence shows someone who is not a quitter? | «He never tried at all.» | *«She kept practising until she could do the jump.» | «He threw his kit in the bin.» | «He gave up halfway and went home.»
exam: Read this: «Nobody wants to be a quitter, but a sensible person stops when it is unsafe.» Why is stopping when it is unsafe not quitting? | It means you never win | *It is sensible, because you stop to stay safe | It means you are a quitter after all | It is lazy, because you did not try
